course: dictionary
lesson: 7800
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word quarry is a good example. «Keep away from quarries and old mines, because rocks fall.» Here a quarry is a place, a big open hole in the ground where stone is dug out.
explain: The same word can be a thing being chased. In a story, «the quarry» is the animal the hunters are after, like a fox running from the hounds. Read the words around it: are people digging, or is something running away?
explain: Quarry can also be a verb, an action word. To quarry means to dig stone or rock out of the ground. A sentence like «The workers quarried granite from the hill» tells you what they did, not where they stood.
explain: The safety clues matter too. «Quarry water is very cold and deep and has hidden machinery and ledges.» A sunny day can fool you, because sunny air does not mean warm water. Stay well back from quarries and never swim in them.
fact: A quarry is a big open hole in the ground where people dig or cut out stone, sand or rock.
fact: In a story, «the quarry» is the animal or person being hunted or chased.
fact: To quarry means to dig stone or rock out of the ground.
fact: Quarries are where building stone such as granite, slate and limestone comes from.
fact: Old quarries full of water are dangerous, because the water is deep and very cold, with hidden ledges.
exercise: «Keep away from quarries and old mines, because rocks fall.» What is a quarry here? | *A big open hole where stone is dug out | A small pond in a park | A kind of school bell | A fast animal that runs from hunters
exercise: «The fox ran fast, with the hounds close behind. It was the quarry.» What does quarry mean here? | The farmer who owns the field | The hole where stone is dug | A loud noise in the woods | *The animal being hunted
exercise: «The workers quarried granite from the hill.» Find and copy the word that is an action, meaning dug stone out of the ground. | hill | *quarried | workers | granite
test: Why is swimming in an old flooded quarry dangerous? | *The water is cold and deep, with hidden ledges | The water is too salty to swim in | The water is warm and shallow | Quarries are always empty and dry
test: In «Teenagers swam in a flooded quarry on a hot day», what does quarry mean? | *A big open hole where stone is dug out | To dig stone out of the ground | Animal being chased | A type of boat
exam: «Sunny air does not mean warm water» in a quarry is a warning. What does it teach you? | *A sunny day does not mean the water is warm, so stay out | Quarry lakes are always warm enough to swim in on sunny days | Rivers are never cold | Hot weather makes all water safe
